        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<h2><strong>How does the machine determine what the signal is?</strong></h2><p>Now is the time to look through real seismic data from Anchorage. You will search through the data to identify earthquake signals!</p>"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "d6mPDWDZpZoaEkv5",
        "title": "Text 3",
        "content": {
          "type": "Text",
          "format": "html",
          "text": [
            "<p><strong>Instructions</strong></p><p>1) In the WaveRunner tile under Challenge 2, pick a station and date range. </p><p>2) Click the &quot;Timeline It!&quot; button in the bottom control bar of the WaveRunner tile. The Timeline tile will display the data for the station and dates you selected. </p><p>3) Use the Timeline tile to search through the seismic data for signals of earthquakes. Be sure to check that each signal you choose matches the shape of the ones above! </p><p>4) When you have found a signal, record its characteristics in the table.</p>"
          ]
        }
